arch("arch.WHOLE", "sc.AUTH;sc.OPERATOR;sc.VERIF;sc.CERTMKT;sc.ENFORCE;sc.INFOCHAIN;sc.TRANSITION;sc.DELEG;sc.SCOPE;sc.CIRCUM;sc.REPORTS",
     "The Regulation as one governance arrangement serving the object stated in Article 1(1): addressing greenhouse gas emissions embedded in Annex I goods on importation, to prevent carbon leakage.",
     "A1.P1;A1.P2;A2.P1",
     "SATISFIED",
     "Explicit couplings exist among SC-AUTH, SC-CERTMKT and SC-ENFORCE (see ARCH-01) and, through the verification condition, to SC-VERIF and SC-OPERATOR (see ARCH-02, indeterminate). SC-DELEG is coupled to the other S only through the empowerment assignments (A28(2), A29(2)) that refer to provisions of those S; SC-SCOPE is coupled through the scope of the Regulation (A2(4), A2(7)) and through delegated acts; SC-TRANSITION is separated in time (A32, A36) and not coupled to the definitive-period S by a qualified relation; SC-CIRCUM and SC-REPORTS are not coupled to the others by qualified relations.",
     "integration_through_distributed_powers",
     "qr.A28_CONFER;qr.A29_ASSIST;qr.A2P11_LIST;qr.A16_ACCOUNT;qr.A19_DECIDE",
     "INDETERMINATE",
     "A single configurational property of the whole instrument is not warranted: the integrated core (ARCH-01) coexists with S that are coupled by distributed powers only (empowerments) or not at all (transitional, circumvention, reports).",
     "Bearer: ARCHITECTURE (ARCH-07). Rule: the coupling kinds of I2 are not an ordered scale; no union of S is taken as warrant.",
     "INDETERMINATE",
     "Closure statement CL-01 and CL-07 (absence of a qualified relation coupling the transitional regime to the definitive regime, within the declared corpus only); unresolved external constitutive dependencies are listed for the S concerned.",
     "ext.UCC_PERSONS;ext.REG182;ext.REG2018_2067;ext.REG765_NAB;ext.REG2015_1222;ext.DIR87_PEN",
     "Rival grouping: one architecture for the whole Regulation; or distinguishable architectures (compliance regime, transitional regime, delegation, scope management). Declared coverage is complete for W, but unresolved constitutive external dependencies prevent a 'distinct architectures' outcome (RGAM-DR-25), and the empowerment couplings are source-supported overlaps.",
     "If the external instruments were resolved, the verification and delegation S could be integrated into the core, and the transitional regime could be recognised as a separate (distinguishable) architecture; as it stands the whole is partially integrated.",
     "INDETERMINATE", "OVERLAPPING_OR_PARTIALLY_INTEGRATED",
     "Overlap is source-supported: the integrated core (ARCH-01) overlaps with the delegation S (empowerment assignments referring to its provisions) and with the verification and operator S (through the verification condition); the intersection is not treated as a new architecture; other S remain unintegrated or indeterminate. The outcome is queued for human review.",
     unc="unc.EXT_POS", hq="hq.OVERLAP_ARCH07")

